      "content": "<h3>Use LinkedList or something else?</h3>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"8\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:100%;\">\n<tr><th style=\"text-align:left;\">Use LinkedList when</th><th style=\"text-align:left;\">Use something else when</th></tr>\n<tr><td>You add and remove at both ends (queue, deque)</td><td>You only need a queue or stack: <code>ArrayDeque</code> is faster</td></tr>\n<tr><td>You insert many times while walking with an iterator</td><td>You read by index a lot: use <code>ArrayList</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>You need one object that is both a List and a Queue</td><td>Memory is tight: use <code>ArrayList</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>The list is small and the code stays simple</td><td>Elements need priority order: use <code>PriorityQueue</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>You must store null in a queue</td><td>Many threads share the queue: use <code>ConcurrentLinkedDeque</code></td></tr>\n</table>"
