      "content": "<h3>29. stream().filter(...).findFirst() and anyMatch</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Signature:</strong> <code>Optional&lt;E&gt; findFirst() / boolean anyMatch(Predicate p)</code></li>\n<li><strong>Returns:</strong> an Optional or a boolean</li>\n<li><strong>Time:</strong> O(n), stops early</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>For freshers:</strong> Find the first group that fits a condition, or ask whether any group does. The Optional answer reminds you to handle \"nothing found\".</p>\n<p><strong>For experienced developers:</strong> Because the stream iterates the list once and stops at the first hit, no extra index access is needed.</p>",
      "codeExamples": [
        "// filter + findFirst on a LinkedList\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.stream.*;\n\npublic class LLStreamFindDemo {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        LinkedList<Integer> groupSizes = new LinkedList<>(List.of(4, 9, 15, 7, 22));\n        Optional<Integer> firstBig = groupSizes.stream().filter(s -> s > 10).findFirst();\n        System.out.println(\"First group above 10: \" + firstBig.orElse(-1));       // 15\n        System.out.println(\"Any group above 50?   \" + groupSizes.stream().anyMatch(s -> s > 50));\n        System.out.println(\"Groups of 5 or less   : \" + groupSizes.stream().filter(s -> s <= 5).count());\n    }\n}\n// OUTPUT:\n// First group above 10: 15\n// Any group above 50?   false\n// Groups of 5 or less   : 1"
      ]
